// case: config-port-not-literal
// what: a `port` config declaration whose value is an expression.
//
// The port is fixed when the program is compiled - it is emitted into the
// server's main, not read from the environment - so an expression cannot
// mean anything here. The reader never runs, and reporting the unknown name
// it mentions would be describing a call that was never going to happen;
// the honest diagnostic is about the declaration, not the name.
port nonexistent_fn()
// expect-error: takes an integer literal
